flowchart TD
    box_0(["Start"])
    box_1["Record the false rejection rate over the last 100<br/>parts and the rejection type (orientation, marking,<br/>presence). Compare with the baseline false rejection<br/>rate from the last successful calibration."]
    box_2{"Is the false rejection limited to one inspection<br/>type (e.g. only orientation rejections or only<br/>marking rejections)?"}
    box_3["Complete the following checks: 1. Access the vision<br/>rejection log and sort by inspection module. 2.<br/>Identify which module produces the highest<br/>proportion of false rejects. 3. Check whether the<br/>rejections correlate with a specific part feature."]
    box_4{"Is the calibration target in good condition (no<br/>surface scratches, discolouration, or<br/>contamination)?"}
    box_5["Inspect the calibration target for surface<br/>contamination, scratches, or colour fading. Verify<br/>that the target geometry is intact and undamaged."]
    box_6["Clean the calibration target with an approved<br/>optical cleaning cloth. If the target is scratched<br/>or faded beyond the acceptable condition limit,<br/>replace it."]
    box_7{"Is the camera lens clean and free of contamination?"}
    box_8["Inspect the camera lens for dust, oil, or<br/>condensation. Verify that the lens protective cover<br/>is intact."]
    box_9["Clean the camera lens with an approved optical cloth<br/>and lens cleaner. rerun ten test inspections with<br/>known good reference parts and measure the false<br/>rejection rate."]
    box_10{"Is the ambient lighting at the inspection station<br/>stable and within the specification range?"}
    box_11["Check the inspection station lighting shielding for<br/>gaps. Measure the background illumination level at<br/>the camera field using a lux meter and compare<br/>against the maximum ambient specification."]
    box_12["Complete the following checks: 1. Measure the<br/>ambient light level at the inspection window with a<br/>lux meter. 2. Compare against the maximum permitted<br/>ambient illuminance. 3. Check the camera mount for<br/>looseness or detectable vibration."]
    box_13{"Is the camera securely mounted with no detectable<br/>vibration induced movement?"}
    box_14["Check the camera mounting bracket fastener torque<br/>and verify that no vibration is transmitted to the<br/>camera from the machine frame during a live<br/>production cycle."]
    box_15["Tighten the camera mounting fasteners and add<br/>vibration isolation if required. rerun ten<br/>inspection cycles and measure the false rejection<br/>rate."]
    box_16{"Has the false rejection rate returned to within the<br/>acceptable baseline threshold after corrections?"}
    box_17["Run the full vision system calibration procedure<br/>using the calibration target and update all<br/>calibration parameters. Notify the maintenance team."]
    box_18[/"Refer to the vision system calibration procedure."/]
    box_19{"Is the false rejection rate within the acceptable<br/>threshold after recalibration?"}
    box_20["Escalate to the maintenance team: the vision system<br/>false rejection rate cannot be corrected through<br/>recalibration; inspect camera sensor and optics for<br/>physical damage."]
    box_21["Record the recalibration date, corrective actions,<br/>and final false rejection rate in the quality log.<br/>Notify quality assurance team."]
    box_22(["End, resume production."])
    box_23{"Has the false rejection rate reached a level that<br/>indicates a vision system failure, where genuine<br/>conforming parts are being systematically rejected<br/>and production viability is compromised?"}
    box_24(["End, vision system shut down immediately: false<br/>rejection rate critical, quarantine parts rejected<br/>in the affected window and escalate to vision system<br/>engineer"])
    box_25[/"Vision system lens and focus diagnostic (GRAPH 37)"/]

